Here is the complete Python script to automatically scan a folder of local images, match them with text prompts, and format them into the exact JSONL format required by Unsloth’s multimodal and vision fine-tuning pipelines.
This script processes popular image formats (.jpg, .jpeg, .png, .webp) and handles the absolute path formatting that Unsloth requires to locate your media during training.
Step 1: Install Required Libraries
Before running the script, make sure you have the standard image processing library installed:
